There is a knock on the door, and Ludwig jumps down from the sofa.
He runs out into the hallway and barks happily.
I open the door, and Nina stands outside with her weekend bag.
"Hi Maya, thank you so much for the help," she says and smiles.
Ludwig wags his tail and jumps up at her.
"Down, Ludwig," Nina says and pats him.
"He has been a really good dog," I tell her.
"He must not eat human food, so I only gave him his dry food."
Nina laughs and takes his dog leash from the small table.
"Did you walk him in the dog forest?" she asks.
"Yes, and he loved it," I reply.
I give her the rest of the dog food.
"Take it."
"You must definitely let me look after him again."
"Only if you really want to," Nina says.
"I would very much like to, next time you travel," I say warmly.
"Come, Ludwig, we must go home," Nina says to the dog.
I wave goodbye to them both.
The apartment is suddenly very quiet without him.
